@startuml class-oai-record
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: one new table, oai_records, holds a projection of every harvestable
'       entry with no foreign key to it (tombstones outlive the entry and its
'       catalog); crosswalks render XML from the projection, so what is
'       served is exactly what was fingerprinted and datestamped.
' Kind: UML class diagram, proposal (IP-033). Scope: new types and the
'       existing models they read. Omitted: unrelated Entry fields.
' Source: apps/core/models/{entry,catalog,category,author}.py,
'         settings EVILFLOWERS_IDENTIFIERS, apps/content/citation.py
'         entry_url; OAI-PMH 2.0 spec §2.4, §3.4, guidelines-marcxml
'         (2026-11-16).
' =============================================================================

title OAI-PMH data model: a projection table and two crosswalks (proposal IP-033, 2026-11-16)

package "apps.core (existing)" as core {
  class Entry {
    id : UUID
    title : str
    published_at : PartialDate
    publisher : str
    summary : str
    identifiers : hstore [isbn, doi, …]
    rights : JSON
    page_count : int
  }
  class Catalog {
    url_name : slug
    is_public : bool
    harvestable : bool «new, Q1»
  }
  class Category {
    id : UUID
    term : str
    scheme : str
    label : JSON
  }
  class Author {
    name : str
    surname : str
  }
  class Acquisition {
    mime : str
  }
}

package "apps.oai (new)" as oai {
  class OaiRecord <<proposed>> <<focus>> {
    id : bigint
    entry_id : UUID «unique, no FK»
    set_specs : text[]
    datestamp : timestamptz «whole seconds»
    deleted : bool
    fingerprint : char(64)
    projection : JSONB «null when deleted»
    --
    index on [datestamp, id]
    GIN index on set_specs
  }
  class RecordProjection <<proposed>> {
    identifier : oai:<repo-id>:<entry uuid>
    title, summary, publisher : str
    authors : [surname, name] in position order
    subjects : [scheme, term, label]
    identifiers : isbn · doi · url
    language : ISO 639
    date : partial date
    rights : licence, access
    formats : [mime]
    page_count : int
  }
  interface Crosswalk <<proposed>> {
    prefix : str
    namespace : URI
    schema : URL
    version : int
    render(projection) : Element
  }
  class OaiDc <<proposed>> {
    prefix = "oai_dc"
  }
  class Marc21 <<proposed>> {
    prefix = "marc21"
    MARC21 slim
  }
  class ResumptionToken <<proposed>> {
    verb, prefix, set : str
    from, until : datetime
    after : [datestamp, id]
    cursor, total : int
    --
    signed with django.core.signing
  }
}

Entry "*" -- "1" Catalog : catalog
Entry "*" -- "*" Category : categories
Entry "*" -- "*" Author : authors (position)
Entry "1" -- "*" Acquisition : files
OaiRecord "0..1" ..> "0..1" Entry : entry_id\n(logical, survives delete)
OaiRecord *-- "0..1" RecordProjection : projection
Crosswalk <|.. OaiDc
Crosswalk <|.. Marc21
Crosswalk ..> RecordProjection : renders
ResumptionToken ..> OaiRecord : keyset cursor

legend bottom left
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | plain class | existing model |
  | dashed, «proposed» | new in IP-033 |
  | dashed arrow | logical reference / dependency, not a foreign key |
  | «new, Q1» | proposed field, depends on review question Q1 |
endlegend

caption setSpecs: "<catalog url_name>" and "<url_name>:<category id>" (ASCII, stable across renames of a term). The identifier's repository part is a\nsetting (prod evilflowers.elvira.stuba.sk, dev its own domain), never INSTANCE_NAME (default evilflowers.local is not a domain).
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersCatalog · docs/diagrams/class-oai-record.puml
@enduml
